critical_operation.description:
processHeaderValue() rejects values containing characters outside the legal header range at line 288, but the special-case Host path in processHeader() copies the raw value into request.host at line 308 without running that regex. lib/client.js then interpolates the stored value directly into the request line: `if (typeof host === 'string') { header += \`host: ${host}
\` }` (lines 1397-1398). A caller that passes a Host value such as `12 

aaa:aaa` therefore injects arbitrary header lines or splits the request, even though the same value would be rejected as a normal header. The 5.19.1 fix adds `if (headerCharRegex.exec(val) !== null) { throw new InvalidArgumentError(...) }` before the assignment.
